														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2854336">
									

<p>This has a lot of tropes swirling around on it. I don't mean to say that they're poorly combined, but that I don't think they're advisable at all. So, this is:<br />
- A magical vigilante with perfect knowledge.<br />
- Its solution to sex offenders is <a href="https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chemical_castration">literally what they already try to do with sex offenders</a>, except in this case it works perfectly, never hits an innocent, and presumably doesn't have long-term health outcomes. Forgive me if I don't find &quot;just like the system, but magic and more extreme&quot; to be a clever ironic comeuppance.<br />
- It also gives them alternative pleasures that act as standard-issue cursed wish-granters/compulsion effects. Which can probably kill them, because execution is fine too, right? Also, I get the feeling that you mean these things are pleasurable but not fetishes/sexual, but the language there should be more distinct.<br />
- All of this is bookended by a meme and an internet fad/movement.</p>
<p>So yeah, it's a bunch of bad tropes stitched together, amounting to &quot;our justice system but with more extreme punishment and without the bad parts.&quot; I'm all for GAW tackling sex offenders, but this just feels like a wish fulfillment power fantasy. -1</p>

							</div>

								
